{
  "requirement": "An application-supplied assessment procedure can perform ordinary computation\nand request zero or more typed model answers. It can use intermediate answers\nin later computation and requests, then return its `Criterion::Ok` value.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover each part of `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.procedures`.\n\nThe procedure under test is `impl[Review/Criterion<Memory>]/fn[execute]`, which calls `impl[Memory]/fn[run_review]`. That function does ordinary computation: it records the node, optionally delays, and builds `Assessment { result: node != 9, rationale: format!(...) }`.\n\n- **Zero model answers.** In `fn[runner_reuses_negative_judgments_and_records_only_callback_observations]`, the procedure makes no `ask` call and no agent is configured. It returns an `Ok` assessment, and the test asserts the result is false for node 9, with `selections` empty and no dependencies recorded. The test also checks that the returned value is a `Criterion::Ok` value.\n- **One or more typed answers.** In `fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` the procedure runs with `ask_in_callback: true`. It makes two typed `ctx.ask::<Answer>()` calls and returns an `Ok` assessment, which the test asserts has a true `.result`. `fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]` also makes typed `Answer` requests, asserting `first.n == 7` and `second.n == 11`.\n- **Intermediate answers in later computation and requests.** The second request's context is built from `first.n`. The test asserts `requests[1].0 == \"Check intermediate result 7\"` and that exactly 2 requests were made. The callback also asserts `second.n == first.n`, so the intermediate value is used in later computation.\n- **Returning the `Criterion::Ok` value.** Both runner tests assert on the returned `.result` of the `Assessment`. The two tests return different values (true for node 1, false for node 9), so the assertions distinguish the procedure's computed output.\n- **Failure case.** Without an agent configured, the test asserts `ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured` is returned and nothing is recorded. That case is covered by other requirements.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation in the subject's text.",
